      "Strings": [
        {
          "Culture": "en",
          "Value": "When the flag is set, the system will automatically split this search parameter into three parameters: \"Exact value\", \"Start value\", and \"End value\". For each value, a prompt will be automatically added to ensure correct filling based on the user's query (only for parameters that are applicable to the user's request).\n\nFor example, setting this flag will ensure correct data search for user queries such as:\n    • Find documents from July (uses the \"between\" operand)\n    • Find documents costing from 10 thousand (uses the \"greater than or equal\" operand)\n    • Find the document created on July 15 (uses the \"equals\" operand)\n    • etc.\n\nWhen setting the flag, it is recommended to ensure that the following operands are allowed for the parameter: equals, between, greater than or equal (or greater than), less than or equal (or less than)."
